-  * `rm /1/var/lib/openlibrary/coverstore/items/l_cover_0008/l_covers_0008_00.*`
+Finalization checks for all four ZIPs in their corresponding Internet Archive
+items. Only then are the cover records marked `uploaded=true`, their `filename`
+fields changed to direct archive.org URLs, and local source images and ZIPs
+removed. Records missing one or more local image variants are marked
+`failed=true` and left out of completion updates. A batch lock prevents archive
+and upload workers from modifying the same batch concurrently. Re-running the
+archive step safely skips existing ZIP members.
+
+The `failed` and `uploaded` columns default to false and have indexes
+`cover_failed_idx` and `cover_uploaded_idx`. `archived` means that the local
+ZIP package was created; `uploaded` means all four variants were verified at
+archive.org. Older TAR-backed records remain readable through the existing
+legacy TAR index path.
